# act (https://github.com/nektos/act) — local GitHub Actions runner.
#
# This file is checked in. The `DOCKER_HOST` env var (which act also reads
# as a daemon-socket fallback) is NOT — set it in your shell. See the
# "Testing CI locally" section in README.md for setup instructions.

# Use the catthehacker images — closest match to GitHub's ubuntu-latest
# runners; smaller "act-latest-slim" works for most jobs but lacks some
# dev tools so we stick with the full image.
-P ubuntu-latest=ghcr.io/catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Avoid re-pulling on every run (the image is ~1GB). Comment out or
# pass `--pull` on the CLI when you want to refresh.
--pull=false

# Reuse containers across runs — much faster iteration since `npm ci`
# and the apt cache survive between invocations.
--reuse
